\subsection*{3. Metric and Gravitational Model}

\paragraph{3.1 Kerr-Schild Perturbative Metric}
The gravitational field is modeled using a Kerr-Schild form:
\[
g_{\mu\nu}
=
\eta_{\mu\nu}
+
2H\,l_\mu l_\nu,
\]
where $H$ encodes perturbative gravitational potential contributions and
$l_\mu$ is a null vector aligned with Earth's rotation axis.

\paragraph{3.2 Harmonic Expansion}
Static gravitational harmonics are expanded to degree/order $N=2190$
using EGM2008 coefficients:
\[
\Phi(r,\theta,\phi)
=
\sum_{\ell=0}^{2190}
\sum_{m=-\ell}^{\ell}
C_{\ell m} Y_{\ell m}(\theta,\phi).
\]

% ---------------------------------------------------------
\subsection*{4. Adaptive Mesh Refinement (AMR)}

AG-CSE employs a multi-level Voronoi AMR strategy:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Refinement triggered by gradients in $B$, $\rho$, and vorticity.
    \item Coarsening applied in smooth-flow regions.
    \item Load balancing performed every 50 steps across 2,048 GPUs.
\end{itemize}

Average inter-node latency:
\[
4.2\ \text{ms}.
\]

